  2	//! Zig std.process.Child since at the time of authoring this, std.process.Child
  3	//! didn't support the options necessary to spawn a shell attached to a pty.
  4	//!
  5	//! Consequently, I didn't implement a lot of features that std.process.Child
  6	//! supports because we didn't need them. Cross-platform subprocessing is not
  7	//! a trivial thing to implement (I've done it in three separate languages now)
  8	//! so if we want to replatform onto std.process.Child I'd love to do that.
  9	//! This was just the fastest way to get something built.
